/-!
# The augmentation of the relative hypercovering complex is a kernel in degree zero

Let `f : X ⟶ S` be a morphism of schemes and `K` a hypercovering of the Zariski site of `X` with
base object the top open.  `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.UniversalPushforward.hypercoveringAugAll` is
the augmentation

`ε : (f_*M)[0] ⟶ 𝓚⁼(K, f, M) = ( ∏_{i ∈ I₀} f_{i,*}M|_{U_i} ⟶ ∏_{i ∈ I₁} f_{i,*}M|_{U_i} ⟶ ⋯ )`

of the relative hypercovering complex, natural in the `𝒪_X`-module `M`.  **This file proves that
in degree zero the augmentation exhibits `f_*M` as the kernel of the first differential**, for an
*arbitrary* `𝒪_X`-module `M`:  no injectivity, no quasi-coherence, no affineness of the members of
`K` and no hypothesis on `f`.  That is the degree-zero half of the relative form of
[Stacks, Tag 01GV], the clause `hker` of
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.UniversalPushforward.quasiIso_hypercoveringAugNat_app`.

Together with the positive-degree half
(`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.UniversalPushforward.exactAt_hypercoveringComplexAll_of_injective`,
which does need injectivity) it discharges the last outstanding hypothesis `hεinj` of the
comparison machinery `StacksDraft.DerivedSectionsComparison` — the construction in the proof of
[Stacks, Tag 09VX] — at the data of [Stacks, Tag 01XN]:  `ε` is a quasi-isomorphism at every
injective sheaf of `𝒪_X`-modules.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.UniversalPushforward.restrictedSectionsCoefficients`:  the
  coefficients of the complex of sections of the restricted hypercovering `K ⊓ f ⁻¹ V`, namely
  the underlying abelian sheaf of `M` read on the slice over `⊤ ⊓ f ⁻¹ V`.

## Main results

* `Stacks.CategoryTheory.FormalCoproductAugmentation.isTerminal_overPost_obj_mkId`:  `Over.post H`
  carries the terminal object `𝟙 Y` of `Over Y` to a terminal object of `Over (H Y)`.
* `Stacks.CategoryTheory.FormalCoproductAugmentation.map_terminalAugZero_comp`:  **the canonical
  augmentation of a Čech-style complex commutes with a product-preserving additive functor**,
  through the degreewise comparison of
  `Stacks.CechPushforward.cochainComplexFunctorCompMapHomologicalComplexIso`.
* `Stacks.CategoryTheory.FormalCoproductAugmentation.terminalAugZero_mapFormalCoproduct`:  **the
  canonical augmentation is unchanged by reindexing the simplicial formal coproduct along a
  functor** and restricting the coefficients along it.
* `Stacks.CategoryTheory.Hypercovering.isIso_kernelLift_terminalAugZeroOfEq`:  the degree-zero
  half of [Stacks, Tag 01GV] in kernel-lift form, at a Grothendieck topology presented as the one
  generated by the pretopology the hypercovering refers to.
* `UniversalPushforward.terminalAugZero_comp_hypercoveringSectionsComplexIso_zero`:
  **the degree-zero compatibility**:  the sections over `V` of the canonical augmentation of
  `𝓚⁼(K, f, M)` are, through `hypercoveringSectionsComplexIso`, the canonical augmentation of the
  complex of sections of the restricted hypercovering `K ⊓ f ⁻¹ V`.
* `UniversalPushforward.isIso_kernelLift_terminalAugZero_pushforwardPresheafAll`:
  **the clause `hker`** — the augmentation of `𝓚⁼(K, f, M)` is a kernel of the first differential,
  at an arbitrary `𝒪_X`-module.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.UniversalPushforward.quasiIso_hypercoveringAugAll_app_of_injective`:
  **the hypothesis `hεinj` of [Stacks, Tag 09VX] for the relative hypercovering complex** — `ε` is
  a quasi-isomorphism at every injective sheaf of `𝒪_X`-modules.

## Implementation notes

The degree-zero compatibility is not proved on elements.  The comparison
`hypercoveringSectionsComplexIso` is the composite of two pieces, each of which is functorial in
the coefficient presheaf, and the augmentation is compatible with each for a separate reason:  with
the first because applying a product-preserving additive functor termwise commutes with the
augmentation (`map_terminalAugZero_comp`, whose content is
`CategoryTheory.Limits.piComparison_comp_π`), and with the second because the augmentation is
natural in the presheaf (`terminalAugZero_naturality`).  What is left is the passage from the
augmentation of `K` at the restricted coefficients to the augmentation of `K ⊓ f ⁻¹ V`, which is
`terminalAugZero_mapFormalCoproduct`:  both are products of restriction maps along morphisms into a
terminal object, so the two agree by `CategoryTheory.Limits.IsTerminal.hom_ext`.

The terminal object at which the restricted augmentation is formed is forced to be the image
`Over.post (· ⊓ f ⁻¹ V) (𝟙 ⊤)` of the terminal object of `Over ⊤` rather than `𝟙 (⊤ ⊓ f ⁻¹ V)`:
`terminalAugZero_mapFormalCoproduct` compares `H(hT.from U)` with `hT'.from (H U)`, which are
morphisms with the same codomain only for that choice.  The two objects are isomorphic — the
structure morphism of the image is `(· ⊓ f ⁻¹ V)(𝟙 ⊤) = 𝟙 (⊤ ⊓ f ⁻¹ V)` — and
`isTerminal_overPost_obj_mkId` is that observation; it holds for any functor, no thinness of the
lattice of opens being needed.  Nothing downstream cares, the terminal object being a parameter of
`Stacks.CategoryTheory.Hypercovering.isIso_kernelLift_terminalAugZero`.

Every step of the compatibility is applied as a *term*, through `Eq.trans` and `congrArg`, and not
as a rewrite:  the two sides are typed at the `sectionsComplex` spelling on one side and at the
`mapHomologicalComplex` spelling on the other, and a motive abstracting both is not type-correct
at `implicit` transparency.  This is the discipline of
`StacksFrontier.CategoryTheory.Sites.Hypercovering.SectionsComplexOver`, whose
`sectionsEquiv_naturality` is the model for the whole argument.

The passage from the sections to the sheaves is
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.UniversalPushforward.isIso_kernelLift_of_forall_sections`, and it is
one-directional:  evaluation of sheaves of modules at an open set is left exact but not exact, so
only a statement about a kernel transports.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 01GV](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01GV)
